--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mutation 3 -- RT-20260817-005 item 1 revert (compare-facet-manifest-staleness.py)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reverts `except (Exception, SystemExit)` back to `except Exception`, which
does NOT catch SystemExit (SystemExit subclasses BaseException directly,
not Exception).

$ diff -u cfms.orig.py plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/compare-facet-manifest-staleness.py
--- cfms.orig.py
+++ plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/compare-facet-manifest-staleness.py
@@ -307,7 +307,7 @@
     # instruction).
     try:
         vfm = _load_vfm()
-    except (Exception, SystemExit) as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 -- see comment above
+    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 -- see comment above
         return _emit_error("validator-import-failed", str(exc))

     try:

Result: `bash tests/facet-manifest-staleness.tests.sh` -- 48 passed, 1 FAILED
(was 49 passed, 0 failed on the unmutated tree):
  FAIL: RT-20260817-005(1) lock: expected exit=3 (never raw sys.exit(7))
        stdout=[] diagnostic 'validator-import-failed', no traceback; got
        exit=7 stdout=[] stderr=[]
This is the exact regression the fix closes: the corrupted-sibling scratch
fixture's raw `sys.exit(7)` leaked straight through as the process exit
code, with NO diagnostic on either channel, once the `SystemExit` arm was
removed.
Restored: `diff -q cfms.orig.py compare-facet-manifest-staleness.py` -> files
identical (no output, exit 0).

