Mutation 4 -- inject real drift into a vendored schema copy
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Appends one trailing space (no newline) to the vendored
plugins/sdd-quality-loop/contracts/facet-manifest.schema.json, changing its
sha256 while the canonical contracts/facet-manifest.schema.json is left
untouched.

sha256 before: 81d4f1621923133e55875621ba81b30ad9d21688d9442c5a371fc1023b4a4c51

$ diff -u vendored-fm.orig.json plugins/sdd-quality-loop/contracts/facet-manifest.schema.json
--- vendored-fm.orig.json
+++ plugins/sdd-quality-loop/contracts/facet-manifest.schema.json
@@ -132,3 +132,4 @@
     }
   }
 }
+
\ No newline at end of file

$ python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/vendor-capability-registry.py --check
vendor-capability-registry: vendored copies are stale: facet-manifest.schema.json
exit=1

Restored: sha256 after restore: 81d4f1621923133e55875621ba81b30ad9d21688d9442c5a371fc1023b4a4c51
(matches sha256 before -- byte-identical). Re-ran --check afterward:
  vendor-capability-registry: vendored copies match their canonical sources; no drift.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mutation 5 -- revert the T-005 ARTIFACTS extension itself, re-inject the
SAME drift as Mutation 4 (proves the extension, not just --check's
existing mechanism, is load-bearing)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ diff -u vcr.orig.py plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/vendor-capability-registry.py
--- vcr.orig.py
+++ plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/vendor-capability-registry.py
@@ -42,14 +42,6 @@
     "capability-registry.json",
     "capability-registry.schema.json",
     "lite-upgrade-reason-catalog.json",
-    # epic-192-a4-facet-manifest T-005 (REQ-006, design.md Deployment / CI
-    # Plan: "reuses Epic A2's already-CI-wired vendored-copy `--check` mode
-    # ... extended to cover three more filenames, not a new mechanism").
-    # Additive only -- none of the three ARTIFACTS entries above changed
-    # behavior.
-    "facet-manifest.schema.json",
-    "capability-summary.schema.json",
-    "context-projection.schema.json",
 )

With the extension reverted, the identical one-byte drift from Mutation 4
was re-applied to plugins/sdd-quality-loop/contracts/facet-manifest.schema.json,
and `--check` was re-run:

$ python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/vendor-capability-registry.py --check
vendor-capability-registry: vendored copies match their canonical sources; no drift.
exit=0

This is a FALSE NEGATIVE: real drift is present but silently unreported --
proving the T-005 extension (not merely the pre-existing `--check`
mechanism) is what makes the three new schema files' drift detectable.

Restored (both files): vendor-capability-registry.py `diff -q` -> identical;
vendored facet-manifest.schema.json sha256 -> matches the Mutation 4 "before"
value. Re-ran --check one final time on the fully-restored tree:
  vendor-capability-registry: vendored copies match their canonical sources; no drift.

